 "notes": [
  "Europe is an experiment: the model was trained on Canada only (2000 to 2019) and runs here unchanged. On these two summer 2025 dates it ranks where fires occurred with AUC 0.88 (Canada: about 0.97) and predicts roughly the observed number of fire pixels. In November it predicts far too many, so no recent dates are shown.",
  "Its daily inputs are rebuilt from Google Earth Engine (ERA5-Land, MODIS) as for Canada. The static layers are stand-ins from global datasets (GHSL built-up land for roads, power lines and buildings; MODIS land cover; WorldPop; MERIT terrain), mapped to the value scale of the Canadian training data.",
  "Probabilities are the model's raw outputs, without calibration.",
  "Fires are MODIS active-fire detections (MCD14A1, Terra, high confidence) on a grid of about 5 km; for the newest days, NASA FIRMS near-real-time detections of the same satellite."
 ]
